1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,942
This is the Bench Mark Infotech I P O,

2
00:00:02,942 --> 00:00:05,574
a S M E issue on NSE Emerge offer,

3
00:00:05,574 --> 00:00:10,219
open from the twenty-fifth to the twenty-ninth of September.

4
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:13,574
The price band is ₹104 to ₹110.

5
00:00:13,574 --> 00:00:19,193
Every figure here comes from the final red herring prospectus

6
00:00:19,193 --> 00:00:21,128
and exchange notices;

7
00:00:21,128 --> 00:00:24,720
the final price is fixed after bidding,

8
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:28,681
so valuations are computed at the ₹110 cap.

9
00:00:29,181 --> 00:00:30,419
First, the business.

10
00:00:30,919 --> 00:00:34,393
Bench Mark Infotech, from Kolkata, designs,

11
00:00:34,393 --> 00:00:38,676
installs and maintains IT and digital infrastructure:

12
00:00:38,676 --> 00:00:41,989
networks, wireless systems, surveillance,

13
00:00:41,989 --> 00:00:45,383
audio-visual set-ups and smart classrooms.

14
00:00:45,883 --> 00:00:49,045
Its customers are mostly government departments,

15
00:00:49,045 --> 00:00:51,944
public-sector undertakings and institutions,

16
00:00:51,944 --> 00:00:53,328
plus private clients.

17
00:00:53,828 --> 00:00:55,428
The financial checkpoint.

18
00:00:55,928 --> 00:01:05,712
FY26 revenue was ₹60.53 Cr, against ₹50.04 Cr in FY25,

19
00:01:05,712 --> 00:01:09,155
a change of 20.96%.

20
00:01:09,655 --> 00:01:16,695
Profit after tax was ₹10.22 Cr, a margin of 16.88%.

21
00:01:17,195 --> 00:01:18,859
The turnaround is recent.

22
00:01:19,359 --> 00:01:24,557
FY24 was a ₹1.48 Cr loss;

23
00:01:24,557 --> 00:01:32,457
FY25 made ₹5.83 Cr and FY26 ₹10.22 Cr.

24
00:01:32,957 --> 00:01:37,523
The offer size at the cap is ₹42.44 Cr.

25
00:01:38,023 --> 00:01:43,551
₹37.40 Cr is fresh issue that goes into the company,

26
00:01:43,551 --> 00:01:50,780
and ₹5.04 Cr is an offer for sale that goes to selling shareholders.

27
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:55,246
So 88.12% of the deal is new capital,

28
00:01:55,246 --> 00:01:59,856
and 11.88% is an exit for existing holders.

29
00:02:00,356 --> 00:02:01,679
Where does the money go?

30
00:02:02,179 --> 00:02:08,208
Of the ₹37.40 Cr fresh issue, ₹30.00 Cr funds working capital,

31
00:02:08,208 --> 00:02:12,099
and the rest general corporate purposes.

32
00:02:12,599 --> 00:02:17,197
A promoter also sells 4,58,000 shares,

33
00:02:17,197 --> 00:02:20,343
about ₹5.04 Cr at the cap.

34
00:02:20,843 --> 00:02:21,845
Valuation.

35
00:02:22,345 --> 00:02:24,908
At the ₹110 cap,

36
00:02:24,908 --> 00:02:33,076
the price is 11.70x FY26 earnings of ₹9.40 a share.

37
00:02:33,576 --> 00:02:37,452
Listed peers trade higher:

38
00:02:37,452 --> 00:02:45,501
Esconet at 15.66x, Dynacons 26.55x and Xtranet 50.87x.

39
00:02:46,001 --> 00:02:48,831
Small S M E stocks also trade thinly,

40
00:02:48,831 --> 00:02:51,889
which a P E comparison does not capture.

41
00:02:52,389 --> 00:02:53,883
Now balance the evidence.

42
00:02:54,383 --> 00:02:55,753
Watch-out:

43
00:02:55,753 --> 00:02:58,219
Recent turnaround:

44
00:02:58,219 --> 00:03:00,411
FY24 was a loss.

45
00:03:00,411 --> 00:03:01,644
Strength:

46
00:03:01,644 --> 00:03:06,713
PAT up to ₹10.22 Cr, a 16.88% margin.

47
00:03:07,213 --> 00:03:08,241
Watch-out:

48
00:03:08,241 --> 00:03:12,765
Government receivables need working capital.

49
00:03:12,765 --> 00:03:13,690
Strength:

50
00:03:13,690 --> 00:03:16,877
11.70x P/E, below listed peers.

51
00:03:17,377 --> 00:03:18,610
Watch-out:

52
00:03:18,610 --> 00:03:19,103
SME:

53
00:03:19,103 --> 00:03:23,293
₹2,64,000 minimum, thin liquidity.

54
00:03:23,293 --> 00:03:24,402
Strength:

55
00:03:24,402 --> 00:03:28,961
88.12% of the offer is fresh capital.

56
00:03:29,461 --> 00:03:30,592
How to apply.

57
00:03:31,092 --> 00:03:35,095
This is an S M E issue on NSE Emerge.

58
00:03:35,095 --> 00:03:37,584
One lot is 1200 shares,

59
00:03:37,584 --> 00:03:43,643
and the minimum application for individuals is two lots,

60
00:03:43,643 --> 00:03:47,647
2400 shares, or ₹2,64,000 at the cap.

61
00:03:48,147 --> 00:03:52,243
S M E shares trade thinly after listing, with a market maker,

62
00:03:52,243 --> 00:03:55,400
so exiting can be harder than on the mainboard.

63
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:56,860
Let's recap.

64
00:03:57,360 --> 00:04:03,097
FY26 revenue ₹60.53 Cr, profit ₹10.22 Cr.

65
00:04:03,097 --> 00:04:11,493
The offer is ₹42.44 Cr, of which ₹5.04 Cr is offer for sale.

66
00:04:11,493 --> 00:04:17,090
Valuation is 11.70x earnings at the cap.

67
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:22,128
The minimum investment is ₹2,64,000.

68
00:04:22,628 --> 00:04:26,802
This video is public-source education from the red herring

69
00:04:26,802 --> 00:04:29,104
prospectus and exchange notices.

70
00:04:29,104 --> 00:04:33,062
It is not investment advice and not a buy or sell call.

71
00:04:33,062 --> 00:04:34,861
Read the final documents,

72
00:04:34,861 --> 00:04:37,740
check live subscription on the exchange,

73
00:04:37,740 --> 00:04:40,474
and consult a SEBI-registered adviser.

74
00:04:40,474 --> 00:04:41,913
Thanks for watching.

